  derived.state and with `gate.sh done`.
  Commands: my own differential fuzz (fuzz.mjs, 'skip' mode) 300 scenarios seed 101 (70 accepted)
  + 250 seed 7; a dedicated leading-byte matrix (lead.mjs: 19 leading byte strings x 4 headers x
  tiers 1/2 = 152 scenarios, incl. raw 0x85, 0xa0, 0x1c-0x1f, VT, FF, CR, BOM, U+1680, U+2003,
  U+3000) -> 0 gate/dashboard splits, 0 locale splits, 0 stats-locale splits.
  Power check: the same fuzz against the attempt-1 behaviour (copy with `sed` back in the
  caller's locale) reports LOCALE-SPLIT on DETAIL:<U+2003> and REASON:<U+2003>quota, so the fuzz
  can see the defect it is hunting. (My first generator was buggy - it produced only NUL files;
  found by that power check and fixed before any result above was taken.)
  gate.sh:219 skip_field = `LC_ALL=C grep -a -m1 ... | LC_ALL=C sed`; parse.mjs skipField strips
  /^[ \t\n\v\f\r]+/ only. The 15-reason set in gate.sh equals the set in parse.mjs and the brief.

