Observations (none is a FAIL; all outside the written scope)
  1. Verdict-header parsing is still locale-dependent in the gate (`field_of` runs `sed` in the
     caller's locale): FAMILY:<U+2003>crossvendor style headers are read differently under C and
     UTF-8, and differ from the dashboard's .trim(). Explicitly out of scope (CD-h class).
  2. Trailing comma in the checks column (`tests,codex,`): gate accepts, dashboard blocks - the
     known pre-existing split, explicitly out of scope. Spaces / case / duplicates in the column
     agree on both sides.
  3. The gate opens a skip record by name after `-f`; a FIFO swapped in between the two would
     block the gate (same pattern as load_verdict for every verdict). parse() is immune
     (O_NONBLOCK + fstat). Unrealistic for a swarm dir; not required by the brief.
  4. Under a mode-000 verdict the gate's own `grep` prints a "Permission denied" line to stderr
     (pre-existing, load_verdict does not silence it); exit codes and verdicts are unaffected.
  5. swarm/codex-check.sh header still says "only after task CD4" and swarm/start.sh still says
     "no second vendor" (the lead's known backlog).
  6. The shipped gate suite leaks ~1 mktemp dir per case into TMPDIR (newswarm has no cleanup;
     the same line is in HEAD) - pre-existing.
  7. TIERS.md line 53 has an odd hard wrap ("blocks. `codex` / only demands ...") - cosmetic.
